conversations.content:
Each Brainfuck command translates directly to one C statement:

```
BF  →  C
>   →  ++ptr;
<   →  --ptr;
+   →  ++*ptr;
-   →  --*ptr;
.   →  putchar(*ptr);
,   →  *ptr = getchar();
[   →  while (*ptr) {
]   →  }
```

Full C program wrapper:
```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
    unsigned char tape[30000] = {0};
    unsigned char *ptr = tape;
    // paste BF translated to C operations here
    return 0;
}
```

Example — BF `+++[>++<-]>.` translates to:
```c
++*ptr; ++*ptr; ++*ptr;         // +++
while (*ptr) {                  // [
    ++ptr; ++*ptr; ++*ptr;      // >++
    --ptr; --*ptr;              // <-
}                               // ]
++ptr; putchar(*ptr);           // >.
```
